      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA MAGNIFICENT DETACHED FAMILY HOME - A PROPERTY OF DISTINCTION AND STYLE\n\nSaint Ronan's, Rockbarton Park offers a rare opportunity to purchase one of Galway's finest detached homes. \n\nSitting on a large south facing corner site, this property offers the discerning purchaser peace & tranquillity while still being within walking distance of every necessary amenity.\n\nLocated in one of the most prestigious & sought after residential areas in Galway, this stunning private residence is superbly positioned just 150 meters from the renowned Salthill Promenade & Blackrock diving tower with its blue flag golden beaches & recreational parks.\n\nSalthill is one of Ireland's premier seaside villages with a host of shops, cafes, restaurants, bars, and the wonderful Salthill Hotel all on your doorstep.\n\nIts idyllic location also offers a huge range of sporting facilities within the Salthill area such as Galway Bay Golf Club, the Galway Lawn Tennis Club & the local GAA grounds at Pearse Stadium and a number of notable national & secondary schools, such as Taylors Hill, Salerno & St Enda's, while still being situated in a quiet residential location.\n\nThis is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to acquire a magnificent, spacious detached family home presented in excellent condition with careful attention to detail and wonderful taste foremost throughout.\n\nInternally, you will be left amazed by the balance of traditional and contemporary styles that create a stunning family home of immense character and charm.\n\nThis home impresses at first glance, and one would be amazed by the superb dimensions and layout of this stunning family home that oozes style and character. Built in 1940, the property was further extended in 1999 and has undergone considerable refurbishment and upgrading throughout the years.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a bright and spacious entrance hall, which leads to a very large formal dining room with a feature fireplace. The dining area leads into the bright and spacious sitting room that overlooks the private rear garden. A second sun-filled reception room allows extra space for hosting.\n\nThe heart of the home is the open plan kitchen & family dining room with a feature Aga stove. A study, a separate utility room, and a guest WC complete the accommodation on the ground floor.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation is comprised of a generous master en suite bedroom and three additional bedrooms, all of which are generous double bedrooms. A beautifully appointed spacious main bathroom completes the accommodation on the first floor.\n\nExternally, the property is surrounded by stone cut walls to the front, mature gardens, well-maintained lawns, and elegant planting with mature trees & shrubbery. There is a sun-filled south-facing patio area to the rear of the property.\n\nThis highly desirable location is also just 15/20-minute walk from the vibrant cobbled streets of Galway city centre, Galway's West End and the Latin Quarter with its many shops, bars and restaurants.\n\nAdditionally, the property is also serviced by excellent transport links bringing an abundance of local amenities to its doorstep, such as the University of Galway and UCHG.\n\nSaint Ronan's is one of the finest and most attractive homes to come to the market for some time and would prove to be the perfect forever home.\n\nKeep up to-date with NEW PROPERTIES by registering your details on our database For Further details please contact our office on 091-564212 OFFICE OPENING HOURS - MON TO FRI 9AM TO 5:30PMProperties can be viewed on our website www.odj.ie NOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars. No person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
      },
